From 7aaf246fa5e7a1882aefc1440b63b9d62d293898 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:00:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/display: hdmi-audio: reject startup without a sink

The HDMI audio get_eld callback currently returns the connector ELD even
when the connector is disconnected. Reject that case with -ENODEV so the
HDMI codec does not open an audio stream without a sink, while preserving
support for a connected sink that exposes an empty ELD.

Change-Id: I0870daeb9733658246a61cdc14796cee42093b24
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:GPT:5.6-Sol
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/613146
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yannick FERTRE <yannick.fertre@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c
index 7d78b02c1446..dc8387442336 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_audio_helper.c
@@ -85,6 +85,9 @@ static int drm_connector_hdmi_audio_get_eld(struct device *dev, void *data,
 {
 	struct drm_connector *connector = data;
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(connector->status) != connector_status_connected)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	mutex_lock(&connector->eld_mutex);
 	memcpy(buf, connector->eld, min(sizeof(connector->eld), len));
 	mutex_unlock(&connector->eld_mutex);
-- 
